<article class="env-proposition" id="0FIU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FIU">Proposition <span data-tag="0FIU">45.14.17</span>.</a> Assume given data (D0), (D1), and (D2') satisfying axioms (A1) – (A8). Then we have a Weil cohomology theory. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We have axioms (A), (B) and (C)(a), (C)(c), and (C)(d) of Section <a href="/tag/0FHA" data-tag="0FHA">45.9</a> by Lemmas <a href="/tag/0FIJ" data-tag="0FIJ">45.14.5</a>, <a href="/tag/0FIL" data-tag="0FIL">45.14.7</a>, and <a href="/tag/0FIM" data-tag="0FIM">45.14.8</a>. We have axiom (C)(b) by Lemma <a href="/tag/0FIT" data-tag="0FIT">45.14.16</a>. Finally, the additional condition of Definition <a href="/tag/0FI2" data-tag="0FI2">45.11.4</a> holds because it is the same as our axiom (A8). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>